{
	title: 'Drafts that follow you, and optimistic sending',
	description: 'Typed text is never lost (tasks/j1/states.md, Drafts and sending). Each session has one draft stored on the host, so a prompt started in the terminal can be finished on the phone; clients keep a local copy (a file for the terminal, localStorage for the web) and sync it when connected, so typing while disconnected is safe too. A sent prompt shows at once, marked pending until the host acknowledges its command id; while disconnected it stays pending and is sent on reconnect, never twice, and the draft is cleared only after the acknowledgement. Reference: the old draft.ts (artifact). Test the loss cases: host restart while typing, disconnect then send, client crash before acknowledgement.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['r6']
}
